ExtUtils::Miniperl: no-op DynaLoader::boot_DynaLoader in a static perl without DynaLoader

perl-cross builds no DynaLoader when usedl=undef; upstream Configure
would, with ext/DynaLoader/dl_none.xs (DynaLoader present, every dynamic
load croaks). Core modules test `defined &DynaLoader::boot_DynaLoader` to
tell perl from miniperl before loading their XS: re.pm (install(), so
`use re 'debug'`), Cwd.pm (XS getcwd), Unicode::UCD. Without it, -6 died
with "Undefined subroutine &re::install" and ran pure-Perl Cwd.

writemain() now emits a no-op boot_DynaLoader XSUB and registers it in
perlmain.c's xs_init when it is given static extensions but no
DynaLoader. miniperlmain.c (no extensions) stays without it, so miniperl
is still recognised as miniperl. XSLoader::load / DynaLoader::bootstrap
then find each static module's <Module>::bootstrap as usual.

The upstream-shaped fix is the real DynaLoader with dl_none.xs (follow-up
issue). Applied by build.sh (patch -p1 in the perl source). homescoop#182.

--- a/ext/ExtUtils-Miniperl/lib/ExtUtils/Miniperl.pm
+++ b/ext/ExtUtils-Miniperl/lib/ExtUtils/Miniperl.pm
@@ -179,7 +179,27 @@
 
 EOF!HEAD
 
-    print $fh xsi_protos(@exts), <<'EOT', xsi_body(@exts), "}\n";
+    # homescoop wasix-perl: a static perl built without DynaLoader (perl-cross,
+    # usedl=undef) still gets DynaLoader::boot_DynaLoader, as a no-op: core
+    # modules test it to tell perl from miniperl before loading their XS.
+    # miniperl (no extensions) keeps not having it.
+    my $no_dl = @exts && !grep { $_ eq 'DynaLoader' } @exts;
+    my $dl_xsub = $no_dl ? <<'EOD' : '';
+
+/* homescoop wasix-perl: static perl without DynaLoader (no-op marker) */
+XS(homescoop_boot_DynaLoader);
+XS(homescoop_boot_DynaLoader)
+{
+    dXSARGS;
+    PERL_UNUSED_VAR(items);
+    XSRETURN_YES;
+}
+EOD
+    my $dl_reg = $no_dl
+        ? qq{    newXS("DynaLoader::boot_DynaLoader", homescoop_boot_DynaLoader, file);\n}
+        : '';
+
+    print $fh xsi_protos(@exts), $dl_xsub, <<'EOT', xsi_body(@exts), $dl_reg, "}\n";
 
 static void
 xs_init(pTHX)
